================================================================================

Phonon-2.5 ONNX
ONNX conversion of FermionResearch/Phonon-2.5, published by enriqueag.

This repository redistributes model weights from Phonon-2.5 by Fermion Research,
which derives from NVIDIA Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3. The weights remain under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC-BY-4.0), see LICENSE.

Changes made in this conversion:
- The FastConformer encoder, prediction network and joint network were exported
  from the transformers ParakeetForTDT module to ONNX (opset 17).
- Each five-value encoder weight row {-hi, -lo, 0, lo, hi} is stored as two
  ternary planes, lo*A + (hi-lo)*B, in one 2-bit MatMulNBits node per linear
  layer (block size 128). The weight values are unchanged.
- The int6 decoder and joint tensors are stored as int8 with their original
  per-row scales and expanded with DequantizeLinear. The values are unchanged.
- The pointwise convolutions of the conformer convolution module are expressed
  as matrix multiplications with the same weights.
- vocab.txt lists the SentencePiece pieces of the original tokenizer.
The scripts in export/ reproduce the conversion. fermion_container.py is
Fermion Research's reader, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The original NOTICE of Phonon-2.5 follows.

